    "checks": [
      "No ADU, accessory apartment, in-law or similar term in the zoning chapter",
      "Closest path 1: a second residential unit in a separate building on a lot with a single-family dwelling, as more than one principal building (300-28A). Needs a land development plan. Yard and other requirements are met for the whole lot. Lot area for two units is not spelled out. Ask the Bureau of Planning",
      "300-44E names this case: parking for a second residential unit in a separate building may be reduced or waived by special exception with a parking study",
      "Closest path 2: conversion of an existing building of at least 2,000 gross sq ft to a two-family dwelling by special exception in R3, R4, RO, MU, C1, C2. Not listed in R1 or R2 (300 Attachment 2)",
      "Accessory uses may not exceed 25% of the principal use floor area (300-16). A dwelling unit as an accessory use is not listed",
      "Each dwelling unit holds one family or one nonfamily unit. Family: relatives plus at most one unrelated person, or two unrelated persons (Art XVII)",
      "Minimum habitable floor area: efficiency 400, one bedroom 550, two bedrooms 700 sq ft (300-30)"
    ],
    "notes": "Zoning office: Bureau of Planning, Department of Community Planning and Economic Development (page in source_urls). Pending changes: none found that affect ADUs. Census GEOID is the 2020 county subdivision code from TIGERweb."
